Answer: If you have both Magma and GAP at your disposal and if the group in question is not of too large an order, there is a neat little trick I've used a couple of times.
Given a group $G$ in Magma, type the following. 
 IdentifyGroup(G);

 This will give you two numbers $a,b$ which identifies the group in the Small Groups Library.
Then you can start GAP and type this: 
